<div class="hero">
  <p class="subtitle">Deep-Dive — Investor-Inspired Agents</p>
  <h1 style="border:none;text-align:center;margin:0;padding:0">13 Investor-Inspired Agents</h1>
  <p>A Board of Directors Where Every Member Has a Different Investment Bible</p>
  <p style="margin-top:.8rem">
    <span class="badge green">13 Agents</span>
    <span class="badge blue">Hybrid Scoring + LLM</span>
    <span class="badge yellow">13 Files</span>
  </p>
</div>

<blockquote>
<strong>💡 What is this?</strong> Imagine a boardroom with 13 legendary investors — each reads the same financial report but reaches different conclusions based on their personal philosophy. Warren Buffett looks for owner earnings and moats. Michael Burry hunts for hidden value others have abandoned. Nassim Taleb checks whether the company can survive a black swan. This module encodes each philosophy as an autonomous agent. They never talk to each other — they vote independently, like a board of directors with sealed ballots. The Risk Manager tallies the votes and applies constraints.
</blockquote>

<nav class="toc" id="toc"></nav>

<h2 id="architecture">Architecture — 13 Philosophies, One Interface</h2>

<p>Every investor agent follows the same structural pattern despite encoding wildly different investment philosophies. This uniformity is by design: LangGraph's fan-out requires a consistent function signature, and the downstream Risk Manager expects a uniform signal format.</p>

<div class="diagram-container">
<pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
    subgraph Value["Value Investors"]
        WB["Warren Buffett\n🏛️ Owner Earnings"]
        BG["Ben Graham\n📊 Net-Net Value"]
        MB["Michael Burry\n🔍 Deep Value"]
        CM["Charlie Munger\n🧠 Quality"]
        JG["Joel Greenblatt\n✨ Magic Formula"]
        AD["Aswath Damodaran\n📐 DCF"]
    end

    subgraph Growth["Growth Investors"]
        PL["Peter Lynch\n📈 GARP"]
        CW["Cathie Wood\n🚀 Disruption"]
        BO["Bill O'Neil\n📊 CAN SLIM"]
        PF["Phil Fisher\n🔬 Scuttlebutt"]
    end

    subgraph Macro["Macro / Risk"]
        SD["Druckenmiller\n🌊 Macro"]
        GS["George Soros\n♟️ Reflexivity"]
        NT["Nassim Taleb\n🦢 Tail Risk"]
    end

    Value --> Signals["Signal Aggregation\n{signal, confidence, reasoning}"]
    Growth --> Signals
    Macro --> Signals
    Signals --> RM["Risk Manager"]
</pre>
</div>

