<h2 id="code-examples">Code Examples — Common Patterns</h2>

<h3 id="example-graham-number">Graham Number Calculation</h3>

<pre><code class="language-python">def compute_graham_number(eps, book_value_per_share):
    """Ben Graham's intrinsic value formula: sqrt(22.5 * EPS * BVPS)."""
    if eps <= 0 or book_value_per_share <= 0:
        return 0  # Graham requires positive earnings and book value
    return (22.5 * eps * book_value_per_share) ** 0.5</code></pre>

<h3 id="example-peg">PEG Ratio with Safety Checks</h3>

<pre><code class="language-python">def compute_peg_ratio(pe_ratio, earnings_growth_rate):
    """Peter Lynch's PEG ratio: P/E divided by earnings growth rate.
    A PEG < 1.0 suggests undervaluation relative to growth."""
    if earnings_growth_rate <= 0:
        return float("inf")  # No growth = infinite PEG
    return pe_ratio / (earnings_growth_rate * 100)</code></pre>

<h3 id="example-magic-formula">Greenblatt's Magic Formula Ranking</h3>

<pre><code class="language-python">def compute_magic_formula_score(earnings_yield, return_on_capital):
    """Joel Greenblatt: rank stocks by earnings yield + ROIC.
    High earnings yield = cheap. High ROIC = good business."""
    # Each metric produces a rank; lower combined rank = better
    ey_score = 1 if earnings_yield > 0.10 else (0 if earnings_yield > 0.05 else -1)
    roc_score = 1 if return_on_capital > 0.25 else (0 if return_on_capital > 0.10 else -1)
    return ey_score + roc_score  # Range: [-2, 2]</code></pre>

